# Stow packages

Each directory under `stow/` is a package. Paths inside a package are relative to `$HOME`:

- `stow/zsh/.zshrc` → `~/.zshrc`
- `stow/yazi/.config/yazi/yazi.toml` → `~/.config/yazi/yazi.toml`

Do not wrap an extra `home/` folder. `install/stow.sh` restows every package.

## zsh (no Oh My Zsh / no Starship)

- `.zshrc` / `.zprofile` load Homebrew `shellenv`.
- Shared snippets: `.config/zsh/{path,prompt,aliases,functions}.zsh`. Machine-only: untracked `local.zsh`.
- `prompt.zsh` — minimal Catppuccin Frappe (cwd, git via `vcs_info`, exit status). No prompt frameworks.
- Aliases in `aliases.zsh` only. Yazi cwd wrapper `y` lives in `functions.zsh`. Keep `zoxide init` + fzf keybindings in `.zshrc`.
- Brew formulae `zsh-autosuggestions` + `zsh-syntax-highlighting` sourced at end of `.zshrc` (highlighting last).

## yazi

- `stow/yazi/.config/yazi/{yazi,theme,package}.toml` plus vendored `flavors/`.
- Theme: Catppuccin Frappe via `[flavor] dark = "catppuccin-frappe"`.
- After stow, `install/stow.sh` runs `ya pkg install` when `package.toml` exists.
- Keep the `y` cwd wrapper in `stow/zsh` `functions.zsh` (not in the yazi package).

## ghostty

Config at `stow/ghostty/.config/ghostty/config.ghostty` (XDG; Ghostty 1.3+).
Never create `~/Library/Application Support/com.mitchellh.ghostty/config*` —
macOS loads that *after* XDG and it overrides Stow (even an empty file is a footgun).

## sketchybar

- `stow/sketchybar/.config/sketchybar/` — Lua config (SbarLua). Catppuccin Frappe in `colors.lua`.
- Minimal items: OmniWM spaces, front_app, wifi (up/down rates), volume, battery, calendar.
- OmniWM watcher lives in `lib/wm/omniwm.lua` (`omniwmctl watch` → sketchybar trigger).
- Requires SbarLua from `install/custom/sketchybar-borders.sh`. Keep `sketchybarrc` executable.

## borders

- `stow/borders/.config/borders/bordersrc` — JankyBorders, Frappe mauve active outline.
- Keep `bordersrc` executable. Started via `brew services` in the custom installer.

## git

`.gitconfig` must `[include] path = ~/.gitconfig.local`. Never commit real name/email.

## Conflicts

If a target already exists and is not a symlink, stow fails. Do not `--adopt` unless the user asks. Tell them to move the file aside and rerun `./bootstrap.sh --only stow`.
